/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:217: What is the difference between validation and optimization?
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:218: Optimization adjusts strategy parameters in an attempt to improve performance. Validation evaluates whether the resulting strategy is genuinely robust and capable of performing beyond the data used during development. Optimization seeks improvement; validation seeks evidence.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:219: Can a strategy pass validation and still fail?
