/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:534: Create a new version instead of pretending the same forward test is still continuing.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:539: According to the Algorier Platform Whitepaper, a trader can describe strategy logic, including entry conditions, exits, risk rules, timeframe, and markets, in plain English. AlgoBuild translates that description into algorithmic logic and brings the generated strategy into backtesting and forward testing.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:542: Describe → Clarify → Formalize → Test → Forward Test → Decide Whether to Deploy
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:545: Algorier’s existing strategy-prompt guidance makes the same distinction: better prompts can produce better-defined strategies, but they do not guarantee stronger performance, and actual evaluation still requires testing and validation.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:546: The goal is a strategy clear enough to test, not an AI that sounds confident.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:547: Start with one trading idea in AlgoBuild, describe it in plain English, turn it into explicit algorithmic rules, and review the backtest and forward-test evidence before deciding whether the strategy deserves further testing or deployment.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:552: Hypothesis → Description → Clarification → Specification → Backtest → Stress Test → Forward Test → Controlled Deployment → Monitoring
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:557: The goal is to produce a strategy clear enough to test.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:561: Start with a trading hypothesis, describe it in natural language, clarify every ambiguous condition, convert the idea into explicit rules, backtest those rules, stress-test the assumptions, forward test the frozen strategy, and only then consider controlled deployment and monitoring.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:563: You need a trading idea, a market and timeframe, sufficiently clear entry and exit logic, defined risk rules, access to the data required by the strategy, and a system capable of turning the rules into something that can actually be tested.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:567: Yes. A prompt can help turn a trading hypothesis into a structured specification. The prompt should identify ambiguity, define measurable rules, and separate strategy creation from actual performance testing.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:570: Do I need to backtest a vibe trading strategy?
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_how-to-vibe-trade.txt:571: If the strategy is systematic and suitable historical data are available, backtesting is an important evidence layer. It does not guarantee future results and should not be interpreted in isolation.
