/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:69: Validation vs Verification: What’s the Difference?
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:70: The terms validation and verification are often used interchangeably, but they describe different stages of evaluating a trading strategy. Verification asks whether the strategy has been implemented correctly. Validation asks whether the strategy is actually worth trading. In simple terms, verification focuses on correctness while validation focuses on robustness.
