/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:219: Can a strategy pass validation and still fail?
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:220: Yes. Even thoroughly validated strategies can underperform because financial markets evolve continuously. Validation reduces uncertainty, but it cannot eliminate unexpected market events, structural changes, or the possibility that a previously profitable edge disappears over time.
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-037r18/pages_text/blog_trading-strategy-validation.txt:221: Can a profitable backtest still fail in live trading?
